p -E 'obo_(queue_oldest_pending_age_seconds|queue_deferred_total|catalog_verified_answers|catalog_hit_rate|discovery_requests_total|db_size_bytes)'` returns all six families. (2) obo_queue_oldest_pending_age_seconds agrees with SQL: `sqlite3 off-by-one.db \"select (julianday('now')-julianday(min(created_at)))*86400 from queue_entries where status in ('pending','deferred','in_progress')\"` within 60s. (3) obo_catalog_verified_answers equals `curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8766/api/v1/stats | jq .verified_answers`. (4) obo_db_size_bytes{kind=\"main\"} equals `stat -c %s off-by-one.db`. (5) `curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8766/metrics/prom` response time stays under 50ms (the dogfood baseline is 14.2ms +/- 6.8 per docs/dogfood/2026-10-16-operator-integration.md:92) - proving the handler does no heavy query.","acceptance_criteria":"/metrics/prom exposes obo_queue_oldest_pending_age_seconds, obo_queue_deferred_total{reason}, obo_catalog_verified_answers, obo_catalog_hit_rate, obo_discovery_requests_total{outcome}, obo_db_size_bytes{kind}; oldest_pending_age matches the SQL within 60s; verified_answers matches /api/v1/stats; db_size main matches stat -c %s; scrape latency < 50ms.","detail":{"spec":"docs/observability-spec.md","sections":["3.4","4.4"],"evidence":"deferred since 11:24:57Z vs newest complete 18:24:42Z"},"worktree":"/home/kara/worktrees/off-by-one-OBS-OB-004","branch":"wt/OBS-OB-004"}
 {"id":"OBS-OB-005","title":"[P3] Get off-by-one into the fleet registry: scrape job, product/service/host labels, and a textfile record for the seed CLI","status":"pending","priority":"P3","complexity":1,"lane":"monitoring","created_at":"2026-11-03T21:05:00Z","updated_at":"2026-11-16T22:57:50Z","capability_tags":["observability","collection","docs"],"reasoning":"WHY: emitting metrics nobody collects changes nothing - the owner's actual question is whether products can be scraped at all, and today off-by-one contributes 0 of the ~20 real application series Prometheus receives. Even after OBS-OB-001..004 land, the series will sit on a loopback port (ss -ltnp shows 127.0.0.1:8766) with no scrape job; the fleet Prometheus config could not be read from this session, so absence of a job is UNVERIFIED but strongly implied. Separately, the `seed` subcommand (cmd/off-by-one/seed.go:172) is a short-lived CLI that prints a one-shot counts summary and exits - pull scraping is structurally wrong for it and it is invisible after exit. WHY THIS ROW IS LAST: it is worth nothing until the endpoint exists; it is worth everything once it does. WHAT: (a) add a scrape job `off-by-one` targeting /metrics/prom with labels product=off-by-one, service=off-by-one, host=<hostname> - OR, if a scrape job is not permitted on fleet-monitor, a local Alloy prometheus.scrape + remote_write sidecar on the off-by-one host (preferred over exposing 8766, because main.go:298 warns the API has no authentication and must not bind non-loopback); (b) for the seed lane emit a textfile/pushgateway completion record via node_exporter textfile or Alloy prometheus.exporter.unix - a completion record with exit status and counts, NOT a scrape; (c) document the collection path in docs/observability-spec.md section 5 so the next operator does not re-derive it. NOTE: the monitoring stack lives outside this repo and is owned by someone else - this row's deliverable is the config change plus the doc, not a change to service code. Spec: docs/observability-spec.md section 5 and section 7. ACCEPTANCE: (1) In Prometheus, `up{job=\"off-by-one\"}` returns exactly 1 series with value 1 and labels product=\"off-by-one\". (2) `count(count by (__name__) ({__name__=~\"obo_.+\", product=\"off-by-one\"}))` >= 12 - i.e. at least 12 obo_* metric families are actually stored server-side, not merely exposed. (3) After a seed run, `obo_seed_completion_timestamp_seconds` (or the chosen record name) advances and carries the run's exit status. (4) docs/observability-spec.md section 5 names the real job name and the real target host - no placeholders remain.","acceptance_criteria":"Prometheus up{job=\"off-by-one\"} == 1 with product=\"off-by-one\"; count(count by (__name__) ({__name__=~\"obo_.+\", product=\"off-by-one\"})) >= 12; seed run advances a textfile/pushgateway completion record with exit status; docs/observability-spec.md section 5 contains no placeholders.","detail":{"spec":"docs/observability-spec.md","sections":["5","7"],"owner_note":"monitoring stack is out of repo scope; coordinate with fleet-monitor owner"},"deferred":true,"defer_reason":"OWNER-GATED/ops: fleet registry scrape job + labels live on the fleet-monitor observability stack (foreign host, fleet config); fleet structure/config is an owner decision per lane-authority."}
