 {"id":"RELEASE-OB-019","title":"[P1] Toolchain floor: go.mod pins go 1.26.9, which carries GO-2026-6809 (crypto/x509 compromised intermediate CA); v0.3.0 assets were built on 1.26.10 but host/dev builds still use 1.26.9","status":"complete","priority":"P1","complexity":3,"created_at":"2026-11-04T16:54:13Z","updated_at":"2026-11-16T19:57:38Z","capability_tags":[],"reasoning":"govulncheck ./... at 57bca46c (v0.3.0 base) reports exactly one finding: GO-2026-6809, Distrust compromised intermediate certificates in crypto/x509, Found in crypto/x509@go1.26.9, Fixed in crypto/x509@go1.26.10, with a reachable trace cmd/off-by-one/main.go:366:30 off.main -> http.Server.ListenAndServe -> x509.Certificate.Verify. Standard-library findings belong to the artifact-build owner, not the dependency owner: no module in go.mod is implicated. Host toolchain: go version go1.26.9 linux/amd64, go env GOTOOLCHAIN=auto, GOVERSION=go1.26.9, go.mod line 3 says go 1.26.9. The v0.3.0 release assets were deliberately cross-built with GOTOOLCHAIN=go1.26.10 (already in the module cache at ~/go/pkg/mod/golang.org/toolchain@v0.0.1-go1.26.10.linux-amd64) so users are not exposed, but every local make build, every make release run without the env prefix, and the deployed service binary still link the vulnerable stdlib.","acceptance_criteria":"Raise the Go toolchain floor in go.mod to 1.26.11 (supersedes the row's original 1.26.10 target: 1.26.10 closes GO-2026-6809 but GO-2026-6859 net/http needs 1.26.11, so govulncheck zero is only reachable at 1.26.11) and pin every ci.yml setup-go input to the same exact patch so CI and local builds share one stdlib; document the GOTOOLCHAIN prefix in the release procedure. Prove: govulncheck ./... reports no vulnerabilities at the new HEAD; a bare make build links go1.26.11 (go version -m); make test green; go vet clean; go.sum unchanged; every setup-go pin reads 1.26.11; cite the green CI run id.","detail":{"fingerprint":"8202a6fb92f50c2c5d3cbdb3122ffdb3a4294ef0e4baead7e52140e4ca928ffc","evidence":[{"run_id":"2aadd1ed","ts":"2026-11-16T19:57:38Z"}]},"foreman_note":"releng re-measure 2026-11-04 tick off-by-one-releng-2026-11-04-16-43-52 at tip fae5f311: govulncheck ./... rc=3, still exactly one finding GO-2026-6809 (crypto/x509@go1.26.9, fixed 1.26.10) with reachable trace main.go:366 ListenAndServe -> x509.Certificate.Verify. Host go1.26.9; go.mod go 1.26.9. Note the shipped v0.3.0 assets were built with go1.26.10 and are NOT affected; the exposure is host/source builds and the deployed binary.\n\ntick=off-by-one-foreman-2026-11-16-19-27-03; worker=openai/gpt-6.1-terra@xkiro; worktree=/home/kara/worktrees/off-by-one-RELEASE-OB-019 branch=wt/RELEASE-OB-019 base=7afc74cd. Worker commit b07ea135 was rebased to 17258b9e onto origin/master after a sibling push (4b82a985); the judged merge commit d9783275 and the pushed 17258b9e carry byte-identical blobs for all five changed files (verified per-file with git rev-parse <rev>:<path>), so verdict 2aadd1ed/PASS binds to the pushed tree by content. Gate evidence on the rebased tip: go env GOVERSION=go1.26.11; go build -o /tmp/ob-rb-verify ./cmd/off-by-one rc0 with go version -m -> go1.26.11; govulncheck ./... -> 'No vulnerabilities found.' (2 findings at 1.26.9: GO-2026-6809 crypto/x509 fixed 1.26.10, GO-2026-6859 net/http fixed 1.26.11); go vet clean; make test rc0 (18 ok, 0 FAIL); go.sum unchanged; 4/4 setup-go pins read 1.26.11. Tier1 guard = DEGRADED PASS rc0 with go_build/go_tests skipped ('No Go files staged' because the worker had already committed) - build and tests were run directly on the committed tree instead, so the gate is real, not a phantom pass. CI run 43944086284 on 17258b9e = success, all 6 jobs, including the job renamed by the new pin: 'Go 1.26.11'. Supersession: the row's original 1.26.10 target was insufficient - 1.26.10 does not clear GO-2026-6859 - so acceptance criteria were re-scoped to 1.26.11 rather than shipping a floor that still trips govulncheck. Judge flagged two uncovered failure paths (a future CI edit reintroducing a floating '1.26'; the README tarball drifting behind go.mod) - filed as TOOLCHAIN-1.","commit_hash":"17258b9ea837358fd9ba10fd80a3dee00fdc0d3d","guard_result":"PASS","ci_result":"GREEN","worker_summary":"Go floor 1.26.9 -> 1.26.11 in go.mod (closes GO-2026-6809 + GO-2026-6859); all four ci.yml setup-go inputs pinned to exact 1.26.11; README prerequisite + bootstrap tarball moved to 1.26.11; GOTOOLCHAIN=go1.26.11 release prefix documented in README, Makefile and CHANGELOG. go.sum unchanged, no source/dependency edit."}
