 {"id":"QA-OFF-BY-ONE-64","title":"[P3] HARNESS: chaos-corruption is N/A ('no db/state files in repo') even though the server creates ./off-by-one.db at startup — corruption/restart resilience is never exercised for the datastore the product actually ships","status":"pending","priority":"P3","complexity":3,"created_at":"2026-11-04T19:14:42Z","updated_at":"2026-11-16T22:57:50Z","capability_tags":["qa-harness","vacuous-cell","database"],"reasoning":"MEASURED battery at 6546b59e00cce3085e1a003bbfe736c0f51db379 (agent cf73b3aa). Evidence row: chaos-corruption N/A 'no db/state files in repo'.\nThe trigger scans the checked-out tree for committed db/state files, but this product creates its SQLite/graph store at runtime: the same battery's errorpath probe log (ep.log) records 'graph store opened: ./off-by-one.db', 'ingest queue ready', 'off-by-one 0.3.0-dev listening on :8766 (db=./off-by-one.db)'.\nSo a Go module whose whole job is a local datastore can never reach the corruption cell — the cell is structurally vacuous here, not a product result. Contrast: chaos-resource PASS in the same run shows the suite-under-cap leg is real, so this is a per-cell trigger gap, not a dead battery.\nDistinct from QA-OFF-BY-ONE-15/-18 (start probe never started the app): there the probe ran and failed; here the cell never enters.","acceptance_criteria":"For a repo whose server creates its datastore at startup, the chaos-corruption cell must generate state by starting the app once (or from a documented fixture), corrupt/truncate it, restart, and grade recovery — or report UNVERIFIED with the named trigger gap. N/A is acceptable only when the product genuinely persists nothing.\nProve at 6546b59e00cce3085e1a003bbfe736c0f51db379 with a corruption cell that either exercises a restart against a corrupted store and reports the outcome, or says UNVERIFIED and names why.\nREJECTS: committing a fixture db to the repo just to satisfy the trigger.","detail":{"fingerprint":"775ae3868283dbe294893cbe234bff30cf0aba6c27e2d15c8125ab27198bcc50","evidence":[{"run_id":"off-by-one-qa-2026-11-04-18-30-03","ts":"2026-11-04T19:14:42Z","tree_fp":"1b5e946c0c6926fbf9b9acea4a75634a171a6774cf2ac86780724431f09dc392","artifacts":["/home/kara/.hermes/cache/scratch/off-by-one-qa-2026-11-04-18-30-03/qa-evidence.jsonl"]},{"run_id":"off-by-one-qa-2026-11-04-18-30-03","ts":"2026-11-04T19:15:23Z","tree_fp":"1b5e946c0c6926fbf9b9acea4a75634a171a6774cf2ac86780724431f09dc392","artifacts":["/home/kara/.hermes/cache/scratch/off-by-one-qa-2026-11-04-18-30-03/qa-evidence.jsonl"]}]},"deferred":true,"defer_reason":"ROUTED to qa-foreman/bunker-qa lane: chaos-corruption cell coverage is a bunker-qa battery defect, not off-by-one repo code."}
 {"id":"OB-OPS-006","title":"off-by-one daemon owns a live SQLite graph store with no backup or restore path (ops census backup P1)","status":"complete","priority":"P1","complexity":3,"created_at":"2026-11-07T20:22:11Z","updated_at":"2026-11-07T20:47:38Z","capability_tags":[],"reasoning":"Measured by the fleet-ops-check tick fleet-ops-check-2026-11-07-16-20-57 on an unattended api_server surface.\n\nCensus: python3 ~/.hermes/scripts/fleet_ops_check.py --project off-by-one --json -> rc=1, kind=service, gap '[P1] backup: owns a datastore with no backup/restore path'.\n\nInstrument is partly a false positive and the refutation matters: two of the three hit paths are NOT the trigger. .coding-hermes/board/schema.sql is the foreman board's own DDL (canonical board is git-tracked JSONL) - refuted. The real store is separate: cmd/off-by-one/main.go:415 opens envString(\"OFF_BY_ONE_DB\", \"./off-by-one.db\") through graph.Open(*cfg.dbPath), seeded from the tracked schema sql/schema/schema.sql (sqlite/Postgres-compatible DDL for problem_classes + lateral edges). A running daemon is live right now: PID 1871714 /home/kara/off-by-one/off-by-one --port 8766 -cron-interval 60s. Whereas most families only have the board-schema false positive, here the database is the lab's product (solved corpus + graph edges), is gitignored (*.db in .gitignore:22), and git ls-files shows NO backup/restore artifact (the only 'restore' hits are answer-corpus JSON filenames). So a disk loss destroys the accumulated solve graph with no procedure to recover it.\n\nACCEPTANCE CRITERIA:\n1. scripts/backup-db.sh exists, takes the db path from OFF_BY_ONE_DB (default ./off-by-one.db), writes a timestamped dump to a configurable destination, and is safe to run against a LIVE database (sqlite3 .backup / VACUUM INTO - never cp of a live file).\n2. The script self-verifies: a --drill arm restores the newest dump into a throwaway database and compares table row counts (must exit 0 and print the compared counts).\n3. docs/operations.md (or the existing ops doc) documents the backup + restore procedure, the restore-verify step, and the schedule owner.\n4. A test proves both arms: normal dump exit 0, --drill exit 0 with matching counts, and a negative control where a truncated dump makes --drill exit nonzero.\n5. python3 ~/.hermes/scripts/fleet_ops_check.py --project off-by-one --json reports no check=backup gap.\n\nDo not 'fix' this by adding a backup for .coding-hermes/board/schema.sql - that path is refuted above.","acceptance_criteria":null,"detail":{"fingerprint":"8aaa3ad6639fa8b200a277ea88ba7c9af4d6105bac6f087eeeb3311a28cc442f","evidence":[{"run_id":"cbe8634b","ts":"2026-11-07T20:47:38Z"}]},"commit_hash":"f91a9852","guard_result":"PASS","ci_result":"SKIP","foreman_note":"Closed by fleet-ops-check tick fleet-ops-check-2026-11-07-16-20-57 (pass 11). scripts/backup-db.sh (online .backup + integrity gate + per-table manifest, 10s busy handler with 3 bounded retries), scripts/backup-db.sh --drill (throwaway restore, per-table row-count comparison incl. FTS shadow tables), --verify <db>, docs/runbooks/backup-restore.md, Makefile backup/backup-drill/backup-selftest. Live proof against /home/kara/off-by-one/off-by-one.db while the daemon ran: dump 56,913,920 bytes sha256 12f1572f..., integrity ok, drill compared all 14 tables -> drill PASSED rc=0 (answer_nodes 4929, problem_edges 11622, problem_classes 3194, queue_entries 5657); negative control 1KB truncation -> drill FAILED rc=1; live file mtime unchanged. Gates: shellcheck -S warning clean, bash -n clean, make backup-selftest 9/9. Census --project off-by-one --json now reports gaps=1 (container P2 only) - the backup P1 is CLEARED. First verdict run cfa8ac76 FAILed only criterion 5 (fix was on ops/OB-OPS-006 while the registered checkout was on master); re-judged after fast-forward+push to origin/master f91a9852 -> PASS cbe8634b. Residual: the daily cron is documented with its line and owner (host owner kara) but NOT installed - installing a host timer is an owner decision, so the schedule arm is unproven.","completed_at":"2026-11-07T20:47:27Z"}
